1
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:11,260
Arnold Swan chocolate.

2
00:00:11,261 --> 00:00:13,847
A treat from the Managing Partner
for everyone.

3
00:00:15,348 --> 00:00:16,808
Thank you, Managing Partner.

4
00:00:19,894 --> 00:00:21,812
- Those cost 2,000 yen each.
- 2,000 yen?

5
00:00:21,813 --> 00:00:25,482
You don't have to hold back.
This is a reward.

6
00:00:25,483 --> 00:00:27,651
It's thanks to your hard work,
Ms. Minamida.

7
00:00:27,652 --> 00:00:30,195
Yes, it's thanks to
Ms. Minamida's hard work.

8
00:00:30,196 --> 00:00:32,906
Hard workers must be properly rewarded.

9
00:00:32,907 --> 00:00:34,617
Keep up the good work!

10
00:00:39,664 --> 00:00:42,917
The Managing Partner
is really soft on Ms. Minamida.

11
00:00:44,043 --> 00:00:47,130
And? The person in question
isn't eating the reward?

12
00:00:47,714 --> 00:00:50,466
If it's a reward, I prefer
the Minami Minamida set.

13
00:00:50,467 --> 00:00:52,176
Minami Minamida set?

14
00:00:52,177 --> 00:00:55,929
A set of three salted rice balls
and sides my dad makes.

15
00:00:55,930 --> 00:00:57,974
But I don't really eat the sides.

16
00:00:58,725 --> 00:01:04,522
You can request that Minami Minamida set
from the Managing Partner next time.

17
00:01:06,274 --> 00:01:08,692
If you want to eat
the Minami Minamida set,

18
00:01:08,693 --> 00:01:10,570
you should come over to eat, Minato.

19
00:01:12,197 --> 00:01:13,948
- I'd like that.
- Huh?

20
00:01:14,574 --> 00:01:15,992
You're calling him Minato now?

21
00:01:16,785 --> 00:01:18,870
Ah, there you are, Ms. Minamida.

22
00:01:20,413 --> 00:01:22,415
I have something to consult you about.

23
00:01:27,295 --> 00:01:29,338
I'm thinking of having you co-handle

24
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,549
a case I'm taking on next.

25
00:01:32,050 --> 00:01:33,801
Have you heard of Fukamachi Biotech?

26
00:01:33,802 --> 00:01:36,595
They handle genetic engineering products.

27
00:01:36,596 --> 00:01:39,097
Fukamachi Biotech. I've heard of them.

28
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:41,600
They're an old client,

29
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:44,395
but the Chairman
recently suffered a tragedy.

30
00:01:45,230 --> 00:01:48,024
His eldest son passed away.

31
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:53,154
It seems his younger brother, who is
a year younger, beat him to death.

32
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:57,617
I'm so tired...

33
00:02:01,121 --> 00:02:01,996
So-chan?

34
00:02:02,664 --> 00:02:04,707
Sosuke?

35
00:02:05,208 --> 00:02:06,667
- Stop it!
- So-chan?!

36
00:02:06,668 --> 00:02:08,128
- So-chan?!
- Stop it!

37
00:02:09,087 --> 00:02:10,462
- No! Why?
- Stop it!

38
00:02:10,463 --> 00:02:12,506
- Sosuke, calm down!
- Stop it!

39
00:02:12,507 --> 00:02:15,176
- Calm down!
- Stop it! Stop it!

40
00:02:17,095 --> 00:02:18,137
So-chan!

41
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:20,222
- It's okay, you're okay now!
- Shunsuke?

42
00:02:20,223 --> 00:02:21,974
- Sosuke, you're okay!
- Shunsuke!

43
00:02:21,975 --> 00:02:23,892
Dear, what do we do! Shunsuke is...!

44
00:02:23,893 --> 00:02:25,435
What do we do? Shunsuke!

45
00:02:25,436 --> 00:02:27,396
Shunsuke? Shunsuke!

46
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:29,189
- Stop it!
- Shunsuke!

47
00:02:29,190 --> 00:02:31,693
I said stop it!

48
00:02:32,610 --> 00:02:36,738
The brother who committed the assault
has autism.

49
00:02:36,739 --> 00:02:37,657
Yes.

50
00:02:41,077 --> 00:02:43,787
The older brother was rushed
to the hospital unconscious,

51
00:02:43,788 --> 00:02:46,832
and died after being in a coma for a week.

52
00:02:46,833 --> 00:02:48,000
The cause of death

53
00:02:48,001 --> 00:02:50,544
was chest trauma causing internal bleeding

54
00:02:50,545 --> 00:02:53,381
in the chest cavity from 22 broken ribs.

55
00:02:54,173 --> 00:02:57,509
Were all these caused by
his brother's assault?

56
00:02:57,510 --> 00:02:58,845
The prosecution thinks so.

57
00:02:59,512 --> 00:03:01,138
The fractures on the front of his ribs

58
00:03:01,139 --> 00:03:04,641
could have been caused by paramedics
performing CPR.

59
00:03:04,642 --> 00:03:06,227
Even so...

60
00:03:06,811 --> 00:03:11,690
the victim also has 11 rib fractures
on his back in a straight line.

61
00:03:11,691 --> 00:03:13,568
CPR doesn't explain that.

62
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:18,239
Why would his brother do
something like that?

63
00:03:19,407 --> 00:03:22,118
Apparently, when asked for a motive,

64
00:03:22,619 --> 00:03:25,662
he only says, "Stop it, stop it."

65
00:03:25,663 --> 00:03:27,706
"Stop it, stop it."

66
00:03:27,707 --> 00:03:30,709
The Chairman's family is coming shortly,

67
00:03:30,710 --> 00:03:32,210
so I want you to meet them.

68
00:03:32,211 --> 00:03:33,129
Yes.

69
00:03:39,677 --> 00:03:41,136
Thank you for having us.

70
00:03:41,137 --> 00:03:42,472
Thank you for coming.

71
00:03:45,308 --> 00:03:47,060
- Come in, So-chan.
- Come in.

72
00:03:54,943 --> 00:03:55,860
Ultraman!

73
00:03:57,153 --> 00:03:58,696
You must like Ultraman.

74
00:04:01,491 --> 00:04:04,243
It's Ultraman Zero. Not just Ultraman.

75
00:04:04,244 --> 00:04:05,328
Zero!

76
00:04:06,120 --> 00:04:07,330
Please have a seat.

77
00:04:07,830 --> 00:04:08,665
So-chan.

78
00:04:10,875 --> 00:04:12,125
So-chan, sit here.

79
00:04:12,126 --> 00:04:13,378
Sit here.

80
00:04:16,381 --> 00:04:18,423
Take off your headphones and sunglasses.

81
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:20,093
I don't want to.

82
00:04:20,802 --> 00:04:21,928
Listen.

83
00:04:22,512 --> 00:04:23,553
We made a promise, right?

84
00:04:23,554 --> 00:04:25,722
Listen. We didn't make a promise.

85
00:04:25,723 --> 00:04:27,432
We don't mind.

86
00:04:27,433 --> 00:04:28,977
Thank you for understanding.

87
00:04:30,979 --> 00:04:32,146
Sosuke.

88
00:04:32,855 --> 00:04:33,940
Hello.

89
00:04:34,440 --> 00:04:36,483
My name is Mr. Miyaji.

90
00:04:36,484 --> 00:04:40,028
- And this lady right here is...
- Minami Minamida.

91
00:04:40,029 --> 00:04:43,365
My name is Minami Minamida,
both forwards and backwards.

92
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:45,367
Kayak, radar, civic, tacocat, racecar,

93
00:04:45,368 --> 00:04:46,869
Minami Minamida.

94
00:04:47,996 --> 00:04:50,915
Actually, Ms. Minamida also has autism.

95
00:04:54,585 --> 00:04:56,837
A lawyer with autism?

96
00:04:56,838 --> 00:04:59,715
We thought she could help defend
your younger son,

97
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:02,050
so we decided to have her
co-handle the case.

98
00:05:02,051 --> 00:05:03,386
I see.

99
00:05:04,304 --> 00:05:05,638
Thank you very much.

100
00:05:06,806 --> 00:05:10,518
Yes, thank you very much.

101
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:14,521
This lady and I

102
00:05:14,522 --> 00:05:17,399
have a whole lot of questions for you.

103
00:05:17,400 --> 00:05:19,402
So, today...

104
00:05:21,404 --> 00:05:22,404
What could that mean?

105
00:05:22,405 --> 00:05:23,823
I don't know.

106
00:05:26,576 --> 00:05:28,119
What's that?

107
00:05:29,912 --> 00:05:31,204
So-chan.

108
00:05:31,205 --> 00:05:32,749
So-chan, stop.

109
00:05:33,708 --> 00:05:34,625
Stop.

110
00:05:37,420 --> 00:05:41,674
Does your younger son
usually get violent like this?

111
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:43,134
No.

112
00:05:43,760 --> 00:05:46,428
He's easily misunderstood,
but he's a very gentle boy.

113
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,805
- Zero.
- He would never attack anyone...

114
00:05:48,806 --> 00:05:49,890
Zero.

115
00:05:49,891 --> 00:05:52,601
Our eldest son also doted on him.

116
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:54,519
They got along very well.

117
00:05:54,520 --> 00:05:59,941
So you have no idea
what caused the assault, then.

118
00:05:59,942 --> 00:06:01,527
Even though he's my own child...

119
00:06:02,695 --> 00:06:04,238
I have no idea.

120
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:08,450
Sosuke.

121
00:06:08,451 --> 00:06:11,496
Do you remember the day
your older brother died?

122
00:06:14,665 --> 00:06:16,500
Why did you hit him?

123
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:18,543
Did your brother do something to you?

124
00:06:18,544 --> 00:06:20,003
Slow down.

125
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:24,217
Like, did he forcefully take
your Ultraman Zero toy--

126
00:06:27,053 --> 00:06:29,180
So-chan, stop!

127
00:06:30,264 --> 00:06:31,556
- Sosuke!
- So-chan!

128
00:06:31,557 --> 00:06:32,849
Calm down.

129
00:06:32,850 --> 00:06:35,895
- So-chan!
- He gets like this when overstimulated.

130
00:06:36,437 --> 00:06:39,232
- Sosuke! It's okay.
- So-chan...

131
00:06:52,745 --> 00:06:53,663
I'm home.

132
00:06:54,914 --> 00:06:57,542
Welcome home, Counselor.

133
00:06:59,335 --> 00:07:01,254
I have a question for you, Dad.

134
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,131
A question?

135
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:06,134
Okay.

136
00:07:09,762 --> 00:07:11,722
What's your question?

137
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:17,395
Do people with autism
ever get violent for no reason?

138
00:07:19,355 --> 00:07:23,150
You're the only autistic person
I know, Minami.

139
00:07:23,151 --> 00:07:26,904
As for anyone else, you'd have to ask them
directly to know for sure.

140
00:07:27,530 --> 00:07:31,450
He has severe autism
with a mental age of 6 or 7,

141
00:07:31,451 --> 00:07:33,244
so he won't answer even if I ask.

142
00:07:33,870 --> 00:07:36,038
Then it might be tough.

143
00:07:37,123 --> 00:07:40,751
Dealing with someone
with autism is lonely.

144
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:42,753
Lonely?

145
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:45,339
We're just a family of two,

146
00:07:45,882 --> 00:07:48,384
but you have absolutely no interest in me.

147
00:07:50,178 --> 00:07:52,889
I change my glasses,
and you don't even mention it.

148
00:07:53,931 --> 00:07:55,515
It was even worse

149
00:07:55,516 --> 00:07:57,602
when you were a kid.

150
00:08:10,907 --> 00:08:14,285
Minami, I missed a step on the stairs...

151
00:08:15,369 --> 00:08:17,787
Look, my forehead. I scraped it.

152
00:08:17,788 --> 00:08:20,583
And my foot... I think I sprained it...

153
00:08:25,505 --> 00:08:26,422
It hurts...

154
00:08:36,057 --> 00:08:37,183
Blocks...

155
00:08:41,521 --> 00:08:44,065
Doesn't he have something he likes?

156
00:08:44,565 --> 00:08:46,525
If you want to get answers out of him,

157
00:08:46,526 --> 00:08:49,070
you should dig into what he likes.

158
00:08:49,654 --> 00:08:50,947
You have things you like too.

159
00:08:51,822 --> 00:08:53,658
I do have things I like. Whales!

160
00:08:54,158 --> 00:08:59,580
I was saved by your
love of whales quite a bit.

161
00:09:02,166 --> 00:09:04,252
Does something hurt? Are you okay?

162
00:09:10,049 --> 00:09:11,675
Excuse me! Let me through.

163
00:09:11,676 --> 00:09:13,843
Minami! It's okay, it's Dad.

164
00:09:13,844 --> 00:09:16,097
I'm sorry. All right, let's go.

165
00:09:27,066 --> 00:09:28,025
My, my.

166
00:09:28,526 --> 00:09:29,986
Minami Minamida.

167
00:09:32,029 --> 00:09:35,700
Are you sleeping flipped over
in a place like this?

168
00:09:38,494 --> 00:09:39,954
Sperm whales...

169
00:09:41,163 --> 00:09:45,126
sleep vertically in the water.

170
00:09:50,172 --> 00:09:51,632
You're good at sleeping standing up.

171
00:09:52,216 --> 00:09:53,300
Now,

172
00:09:53,301 --> 00:09:56,971
shall we migrate to the Sea of Okhotsk?

173
00:09:58,097 --> 00:09:58,931
I apologize.

174
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:01,225
I am so very sorry.

175
00:10:01,726 --> 00:10:03,561
Let's go, Minami Minamida.

176
00:10:06,897 --> 00:10:10,026
Well, it'll take a lot of patience.

177
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:15,072
But that's what communication
is all about.

178
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,375
Do I really have to do this?

179
00:10:27,376 --> 00:10:28,501
You have to do it.

180
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:29,837
Excuse us.

181
00:10:34,425 --> 00:10:37,135
Hello, Sosuke!

182
00:10:37,136 --> 00:10:39,220
A special guest has come

183
00:10:39,221 --> 00:10:41,389
to see you today, Sosuke!

184
00:10:41,390 --> 00:10:42,642
Sit there.

185
00:10:45,853 --> 00:10:46,896
Please, have a seat.

186
00:10:50,399 --> 00:10:51,399
So-chan, over here.

187
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:52,318
Over here?

188
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:55,988
Sit here.

189
00:11:00,034 --> 00:11:03,537
Now, please welcome our special guest!

190
00:11:06,832 --> 00:11:08,625
I am Zero!

191
00:11:08,626 --> 00:11:10,711
Ultraman Zero!

192
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:16,884
Wow, Ultraman Zero
has come to see you, Sosuke!

193
00:11:27,186 --> 00:11:28,270
Look out!

194
00:12:07,017 --> 00:12:09,936
All right, let's all call Zero's name

195
00:12:09,937 --> 00:12:11,646
and send him power!

196
00:12:11,647 --> 00:12:13,274
Ready, go!

197
00:12:17,069 --> 00:12:20,697
Let's all call Zero's name
and send him power!

198
00:12:20,698 --> 00:12:22,407
- Ready, go!
- What are they doing?

199
00:12:22,408 --> 00:12:26,369
She says it's a strategy
to get the client to open up.

200
00:12:26,370 --> 00:12:29,206
Go, Ultraman Zero!

201
00:12:42,386 --> 00:12:43,429
It's not working...

202
00:12:54,064 --> 00:12:57,109
Mr. Miyaji, use your beam!
Um, the Wide Zero Shot!

203
00:13:07,745 --> 00:13:08,954
You got me!

204
00:13:13,167 --> 00:13:14,460
You're 20,000 years too early!

205
00:13:16,837 --> 00:13:18,129
He seems to like it.

206
00:13:18,130 --> 00:13:19,756
Play! Zero!

207
00:13:19,757 --> 00:13:20,757
- Play!
- Sosuke...

208
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:21,966
We'll do it one more time.

209
00:13:21,967 --> 00:13:22,884
Yes, do it!

210
00:13:22,885 --> 00:13:24,427
Zero! Do it!

211
00:13:24,428 --> 00:13:26,721
No. We'll play Ultraman Zero

212
00:13:26,722 --> 00:13:29,432
after you answer our questions.

213
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:31,352
- Zero!
- First, please answer.

214
00:13:31,852 --> 00:13:33,562
Why did you hit your brother?

215
00:13:39,401 --> 00:13:40,819
Ms. Minamida, let's call it here.

216
00:13:41,403 --> 00:13:42,987
Please answer.

217
00:13:42,988 --> 00:13:44,989
What did your brother do to you?

218
00:13:44,990 --> 00:13:46,950
Stop it!

219
00:13:46,951 --> 00:13:49,703
- Stop it!
- It's okay, So-chan.

220
00:13:50,287 --> 00:13:53,790
I'm sorry. It might be impossible for him
to answer questions after all.

221
00:13:53,791 --> 00:13:56,417
- And it was going so well, too.
- So-chan, stop.

222
00:13:56,418 --> 00:14:00,673
- Stop it!
- So-chan, it's okay.

223
00:14:03,509 --> 00:14:07,387
The police have finished investigating
the older brother's room, right?

224
00:14:07,388 --> 00:14:09,557
Will we find anything if we search it now?

225
00:14:10,057 --> 00:14:11,224
On-site police investigation

226
00:14:11,225 --> 00:14:13,810
was for suspicion of assault,

227
00:14:13,811 --> 00:14:15,770
not murder or manslaughter.

228
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,606
The investigation
might not have been thorough.

229
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:20,067
I see.

230
00:14:22,695 --> 00:14:23,988
Funai?

231
00:14:24,822 --> 00:14:25,906
Long time no see!

232
00:14:26,866 --> 00:14:29,200
Oh, do you live around here?

233
00:14:29,201 --> 00:14:30,661
No, I'm here for work.

234
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:32,078
Oh, I see.

235
00:14:32,079 --> 00:14:33,455
What work?

236
00:14:41,881 --> 00:14:44,632
Are you still doing that volunteer work
for the disabled?

237
00:14:44,633 --> 00:14:46,051
It's not like that.

238
00:14:47,052 --> 00:14:49,930
We have to go, or we'll be late. Let's go.

239
00:14:51,640 --> 00:14:52,807
See you.

240
00:14:52,808 --> 00:14:53,726
Yeah.

241
00:14:56,937 --> 00:15:00,732
Um, that was a classmate from college.
Sorry about what she said.

242
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,817
It's fine.

243
00:15:06,280 --> 00:15:08,240
Everything has been left as it was.

244
00:15:08,741 --> 00:15:10,074
Let me know when you're done.

245
00:15:10,075 --> 00:15:10,993
Thank you.

246
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:32,096
When the parents came home,

247
00:15:32,097 --> 00:15:34,182
Sosuke was straddling his older brother

248
00:15:34,183 --> 00:15:36,852
right under this beam
and hitting him, right?

249
00:15:40,731 --> 00:15:42,816
With his back to the entrance. So...

250
00:15:44,902 --> 00:15:45,778
Like this?

251
00:15:46,278 --> 00:15:47,112
Yes.

252
00:15:47,863 --> 00:15:49,031
If that's the case,

253
00:15:50,908 --> 00:15:53,077
the older brother would be like this.

254
00:15:53,577 --> 00:15:54,745
That's right.

255
00:15:57,623 --> 00:15:58,874
What happened

256
00:15:59,375 --> 00:16:01,125
between them before this?

257
00:16:01,126 --> 00:16:03,504
The reason for "Stop it, stop it," right.

258
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,475
Minato, please play the role
of the older brother.

259
00:16:18,102 --> 00:16:21,855
For example, they fought over
the Ultraman Zero toy.

260
00:16:24,942 --> 00:16:26,694
Let me borrow that Zero for a bit.

261
00:16:27,987 --> 00:16:30,446
Stop it! Stop it!

262
00:16:30,447 --> 00:16:32,825
Stop it!

263
00:16:35,577 --> 00:16:36,495
I'll grab it.

264
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:42,876
Sorry, this was in front of it.

265
00:16:49,383 --> 00:16:50,426
I got it.

266
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:53,011
Ms. Minamida?

267
00:16:53,012 --> 00:16:56,180
This electrical cord
is bent in two places.

268
00:16:56,181 --> 00:16:59,101
As if some heavy tension
was applied to it.

269
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:07,483
This width is exactly the same size
as that beam.

270
00:17:07,484 --> 00:17:09,278
Can I take it for a moment?

271
00:17:13,949 --> 00:17:15,283
The death certificate

272
00:17:15,284 --> 00:17:19,079
mentions some kind of mark
left on the victim's neck.

273
00:17:19,705 --> 00:17:22,916
Was the older brother
trying to hang himself with this?

274
00:17:29,590 --> 00:17:30,590
I see!

275
00:17:30,591 --> 00:17:33,176
Sosuke's "Stop it, stop it"

276
00:17:33,177 --> 00:17:35,094
wasn't because his brother hurt him.

277
00:17:35,095 --> 00:17:37,931
He was trying to stop
his brother's actions.

278
00:17:44,271 --> 00:17:45,814
Stop it!

279
00:17:47,608 --> 00:17:49,777
Stop it!

280
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:51,862
Stop it!

281
00:17:52,613 --> 00:17:55,657
There might be other clues left behind.

282
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:03,372
What's this?

283
00:18:03,373 --> 00:18:06,376
This is Shunsuke's notebook
that was left in his room.

284
00:18:13,092 --> 00:18:15,134
It seems your eldest son wrote

285
00:18:15,135 --> 00:18:16,344
his thoughts

286
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:19,598
and words of encouragement
in this notebook between study sessions.

287
00:18:22,267 --> 00:18:24,937
We believe these are recent entries.

288
00:18:26,105 --> 00:18:28,357
Please look at the last page he wrote.

289
00:18:34,863 --> 00:18:37,658
I CAN'T SEE THE END.
I JUST WANT TO ESCAPE.

290
00:18:42,037 --> 00:18:42,996
<i>It's too hard.</i>

291
00:18:45,415 --> 00:18:48,335
<i>If I don't try harder,
I'll be left behind.</i>

292
00:18:52,089 --> 00:18:54,591
<i>The exams will keep coming,</i>

293
00:18:55,342 --> 00:18:58,178
<i>and I'll fail again.</i>

294
00:19:01,056 --> 00:19:02,099
<i>I guess</i>

295
00:19:03,058 --> 00:19:04,518
<i>dying is the only way out.</i>

296
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,480
<i>The only way out...</i>

297
00:19:11,942 --> 00:19:14,110
Is it possible

298
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:16,780
your eldest son was trying
to commit suicide that day?

299
00:19:17,322 --> 00:19:20,033
This electrical cord was in his room.

300
00:19:20,534 --> 00:19:23,704
We believe he may have been trying
to hang himself with it.

301
00:19:24,997 --> 00:19:28,167
Sosuke must have happened to see it.

302
00:19:28,625 --> 00:19:32,086
And Sosuke must have gotten violent

303
00:19:32,087 --> 00:19:34,881
because he couldn't bear to see
his beloved older brother

304
00:19:34,882 --> 00:19:36,215
trying to take his own life.

305
00:19:36,216 --> 00:19:38,594
- And that caused him to panic...
- Shunsuke...

306
00:19:39,678 --> 00:19:40,678
would never kill himself.

307
00:19:40,679 --> 00:19:41,929
But...

308
00:19:41,930 --> 00:19:45,141
Everyone vents their feelings
in a diary or online

309
00:19:45,142 --> 00:19:46,560
when they're struggling, right?

310
00:19:52,774 --> 00:19:53,692
Sosuke.

311
00:20:02,326 --> 00:20:03,827
Did you see

312
00:20:04,494 --> 00:20:08,749
your older brother
trying to kill himself that day?

313
00:20:10,500 --> 00:20:11,335
Yes.

314
00:20:16,590 --> 00:20:17,424
That's impossible.

315
00:20:18,258 --> 00:20:20,427
Huh? But he just said "Yes."

316
00:20:28,727 --> 00:20:29,811
So-chan.

317
00:20:31,939 --> 00:20:33,732
Did your brother try to kill himself?

318
00:20:36,151 --> 00:20:36,985
Yes.

319
00:20:37,945 --> 00:20:38,904
So-chan.

320
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:42,157
Did your brother try to live?

321
00:20:42,991 --> 00:20:43,992
Yes.

322
00:20:44,826 --> 00:20:47,996
Your brother never tried to kill himself?

323
00:20:48,580 --> 00:20:49,414
Yes.

324
00:20:54,962 --> 00:20:57,088
Communicating in a way
that matches his level

325
00:20:57,089 --> 00:20:59,841
is still difficult even for us.

326
00:21:02,177 --> 00:21:04,762
But if we examine this cord closely...

327
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,974
There's no need for that.

328
00:21:08,558 --> 00:21:11,478
You don't have to disgrace our dead son.

329
00:21:13,480 --> 00:21:16,775
What about the honor of the son
who's still alive?

330
00:21:17,359 --> 00:21:21,028
You must prove he didn't beat
his brother to death for no reason

331
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,614
- just because he has autism.
- Shut up!

332
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:25,951
You're autistic too, aren't you?

333
00:21:26,535 --> 00:21:27,743
Who do you think you are?

334
00:21:27,744 --> 00:21:28,870
Um...

335
00:21:30,998 --> 00:21:33,250
Please... just go home for today.

336
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:44,552
What's up?

337
00:21:44,553 --> 00:21:46,345
I heard you made the client angry.

338
00:21:46,346 --> 00:21:47,930
Ah, yeah.

339
00:21:47,931 --> 00:21:50,517
You have to maneuver these things better.

340
00:21:51,435 --> 00:21:54,521
Well, I guess that's not easy
with Ms. Minamida around.

341
00:21:56,648 --> 00:21:57,899
Anyway, I'm heading home.

342
00:22:02,446 --> 00:22:03,655
Have a good evening.

343
00:22:09,703 --> 00:22:12,914
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

344
00:22:15,375 --> 00:22:18,920
GREAT WORK TODAY. ALSO,
ABOUT MY ACQUAINTANCE BEING RUDE EARLIER...

345
00:22:28,972 --> 00:22:31,391
What am I even trying to do
by apologizing...

346
00:22:32,059 --> 00:22:34,143
<i>In the case of the 23-year-old</i>

347
00:22:34,144 --> 00:22:37,563
<i>indicted for beating
his older brother to death.</i>

348
00:22:37,564 --> 00:22:42,234
<i>Since the younger brother
was diagnosed with autism,</i>

349
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:44,862
<i>various opinions are circulating online.</i>

350
00:22:44,863 --> 00:22:47,531
<i>Of course, disability and crime</i>

351
00:22:47,532 --> 00:22:50,367
<i>are separate issues.</i>

352
00:22:50,368 --> 00:22:53,038
<i>However, considering this case...</i>

353
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:02,129
24-YEAR-OLD DIES AT HOME:
AUTISTIC BROTHER ACCUSED OF ASSAULT

354
00:23:02,130 --> 00:23:05,591
IT'S A LOSS TO SOCIETY THAT A BRIGHT
YOUNG MAN DIED INSTEAD OF THE DISABLED GUY

355
00:23:05,592 --> 00:23:08,386
HE'S DEFINITELY GOING TO THE PSYCH WARD

356
00:23:12,057 --> 00:23:14,142
IT CAN'T BE HELPED BECAUSE HE'S AUTISTIC

357
00:23:20,273 --> 00:23:23,527
THE PEOPLE AROUND HIM NEED TO TAKE
RESPONSIBILITY AND SUPERVISE HIM

358
00:23:28,949 --> 00:23:32,035
IT'S SCARY. DON'T WE NEED MEASURES
CLOSER TO ISOLATION?

359
00:23:42,337 --> 00:23:44,130
Hey, buddy.

360
00:23:44,131 --> 00:23:47,383
No! Don't just wander off!

361
00:23:47,384 --> 00:23:49,468
- No!
- Hey, buddy.

362
00:23:49,469 --> 00:23:51,179
- You haven't paid the fare yet.
- Sosuke?

363
00:23:52,180 --> 00:23:53,765
Hey, buddy. Hey?

364
00:23:54,474 --> 00:23:57,144
Hey? You haven't paid the fare yet.

365
00:23:57,644 --> 00:23:59,938
Buddy! Listen to me!

366
00:24:03,316 --> 00:24:04,151
What happened?

367
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:10,532
Sosuke?

368
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,910
- Hey!
- Did something happen?

369
00:24:15,412 --> 00:24:16,370
Do you know him?

370
00:24:16,371 --> 00:24:17,454
Yes.

371
00:24:17,455 --> 00:24:20,040
This guy suddenly got in my taxi

372
00:24:20,041 --> 00:24:23,169
and said he was going to this law firm,
so I brought him here.

373
00:24:23,170 --> 00:24:28,299
I told him the fare, but he started
saying, "Zero, zero." I'm at a loss.

374
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:29,300
I'll pay for him.

375
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:30,302
Zero.

376
00:24:31,386 --> 00:24:33,180
Thank you. That helps a lot.

377
00:24:34,723 --> 00:24:36,308
Zero!

378
00:24:36,933 --> 00:24:38,684
Let's head inside the office for now.

379
00:24:38,685 --> 00:24:39,853
Okay.

380
00:24:42,063 --> 00:24:43,273
Sosuke.

381
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:45,650
Belial is over there!

382
00:24:46,151 --> 00:24:48,361
What?! Belial! Okay!

383
00:24:48,945 --> 00:24:50,696
Who are you?

384
00:24:50,697 --> 00:24:52,573
My name is Zero!

385
00:24:52,574 --> 00:24:53,867
The son of Seven!

386
00:24:57,829 --> 00:24:58,996
Sosuke.

387
00:24:58,997 --> 00:25:00,956
Sosuke, can you attack me

388
00:25:00,957 --> 00:25:03,459
right here with the Big Bang Zero?

389
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:05,170
- Right here.
- They're here.

390
00:25:07,547 --> 00:25:08,632
So-chan.

391
00:25:10,508 --> 00:25:11,551
Mom!

392
00:25:15,096 --> 00:25:17,265
You can't just wander off on your own.

393
00:25:19,976 --> 00:25:22,937
I'm so sorry for the trouble he caused.

394
00:25:22,938 --> 00:25:24,689
I'm just glad nothing happened.

395
00:25:25,732 --> 00:25:26,733
Um...

396
00:25:27,484 --> 00:25:29,277
about my husband being rude the other day...

397
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:31,780
Oh... no, it's fine.

398
00:25:32,614 --> 00:25:34,616
I shouldn't say this,

399
00:25:35,575 --> 00:25:37,077
but meeting you

400
00:25:37,869 --> 00:25:40,038
left my husband and me feeling conflicted.

401
00:25:41,373 --> 00:25:43,040
Even though you have the same autism,

402
00:25:43,041 --> 00:25:45,418
you're so different from our son.

403
00:25:47,879 --> 00:25:51,883
I want you all to handle this case.

404
00:25:55,136 --> 00:25:56,304
However...

405
00:25:57,597 --> 00:25:58,640
I would like to ask

406
00:26:00,684 --> 00:26:02,686
that you do so without revealing

407
00:26:03,186 --> 00:26:05,146
that Shunsuke made that kind of choice.

408
00:26:05,897 --> 00:26:06,731
Yes.

409
00:26:09,192 --> 00:26:12,112
We won't reveal anything
that could dishonor your eldest son.

410
00:26:13,280 --> 00:26:14,531
Thank you.

411
00:26:22,747 --> 00:26:24,958
COURTHOUSE

412
00:26:29,713 --> 00:26:30,713
FIRST TRIAL: WITNESS EXAM

413
00:26:30,714 --> 00:26:32,424
I think the defendant panicked.

414
00:26:33,717 --> 00:26:36,428
What do you mean by panic?

415
00:26:37,012 --> 00:26:39,722
It's common in people with autism.

416
00:26:39,723 --> 00:26:42,266
Unable to withstand stress
or sudden strong stimuli,

417
00:26:42,267 --> 00:26:45,520
they fall into a state
of extreme confusion.

418
00:26:47,188 --> 00:26:48,023
So

419
00:26:48,857 --> 00:26:52,026
the defendant's action
of hitting his brother

420
00:26:52,027 --> 00:26:55,447
occurred in a situation where it was
difficult to control his own behavior.

421
00:26:56,156 --> 00:26:58,365
In other words, at the time,

422
00:26:58,366 --> 00:27:01,493
the defendant's ability
to control his actions

423
00:27:01,494 --> 00:27:05,956
was diminished due to a panic commonly
experienced by people with autism?

424
00:27:05,957 --> 00:27:07,751
I believe so.

425
00:27:10,712 --> 00:27:11,713
Nothing further.

426
00:27:13,840 --> 00:27:17,844
Witness, you are a psychiatrist
specializing in autism, correct?

427
00:27:18,595 --> 00:27:20,012
Well... yes.

428
00:27:20,013 --> 00:27:20,930
In that case,

429
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:25,226
can you tell us how many autistic people
are in this courtroom right now?

430
00:27:26,770 --> 00:27:29,480
What about the attorney
who questioned you?

431
00:27:29,481 --> 00:27:30,690
Objection.

432
00:27:31,399 --> 00:27:35,111
The prosecutor is insulting the defense
with discriminatory remarks.

433
00:27:36,196 --> 00:27:37,030
Overruled.

434
00:27:37,739 --> 00:27:39,823
I understand your point,

435
00:27:39,824 --> 00:27:42,327
but I can't say
it's completely irrelevant.

436
00:27:42,994 --> 00:27:45,037
Prosecutor, mind your phrasing.

437
00:27:45,038 --> 00:27:45,997
Yes, Your Honor.

438
00:27:47,207 --> 00:27:50,835
Does the defense attorney
who just questioned you have autism?

439
00:27:55,256 --> 00:27:59,176
I've heard the attorney over there
has autism.

440
00:27:59,177 --> 00:28:00,220
And do you believe

441
00:28:00,845 --> 00:28:02,679
the defendant had a diminished capacity

442
00:28:02,680 --> 00:28:06,266
to control his actions
at the time of the crime?

443
00:28:06,267 --> 00:28:07,184
Yes.

444
00:28:07,185 --> 00:28:10,479
You claim diminished capacity
because he has autism?

445
00:28:10,480 --> 00:28:11,397
Yes.

446
00:28:11,398 --> 00:28:12,314
But...

447
00:28:12,315 --> 00:28:14,942
Is the defense attorney also in a state
of diminished capacity?

448
00:28:14,943 --> 00:28:15,860
Objection!

449
00:28:16,611 --> 00:28:19,822
The defense attorney's circumstances
are irrelevant to the case.

450
00:28:19,823 --> 00:28:21,156
They're not irrelevant.

451
00:28:21,157 --> 00:28:25,411
The defense argues for leniency
due to autism.

452
00:28:25,412 --> 00:28:28,122
If the defendant has diminished capacity
due to autism,

453
00:28:28,123 --> 00:28:30,582
doesn't the defense attorney as well?

454
00:28:30,583 --> 00:28:32,209
Diminished capacity is judged

455
00:28:32,210 --> 00:28:34,753
based on the circumstances
at the time of the crime.

456
00:28:34,754 --> 00:28:36,171
Autism

457
00:28:36,172 --> 00:28:39,633
doesn't automatically mean
diminished capacity.

458
00:28:39,634 --> 00:28:44,513
You argue the autistic defendant
deserves leniency,

459
00:28:44,514 --> 00:28:48,892
yet demand the autistic lawyer
be treated equally to other lawyers?

460
00:28:48,893 --> 00:28:50,352
Isn't that strange?

461
00:28:50,353 --> 00:28:51,353
Prosecutor.

462
00:28:51,354 --> 00:28:56,401
I'm simply pointing out a contradiction
in the defense's argument.

463
00:28:56,901 --> 00:28:58,278
Nothing further.

464
00:29:12,375 --> 00:29:14,877
That prosecutor's logic
is completely absurd.

465
00:29:14,878 --> 00:29:19,089
He doesn't understand Autism Spectrum
Disorder or diminished capacity at all.

466
00:29:19,090 --> 00:29:20,257
Mr. Miyaji.

467
00:29:20,258 --> 00:29:21,176
Yes.

468
00:29:22,218 --> 00:29:23,553
I'm sorry,

469
00:29:24,512 --> 00:29:28,767
but could you please take
Ms. Minamida off the case going forward?

470
00:29:30,226 --> 00:29:33,480
Of course, I know
she's worked hard for us.

471
00:29:33,980 --> 00:29:37,358
But when the prosecutor
attacks us like that...

472
00:29:38,109 --> 00:29:41,070
That's just their strategy to shake us up.

473
00:29:41,905 --> 00:29:43,864
The defendant's diminished capacity

474
00:29:43,865 --> 00:29:46,784
won't be rejected just because
his attorney has autism.

475
00:29:46,785 --> 00:29:48,911
That logic wouldn't hold up.

476
00:29:48,912 --> 00:29:50,078
Please understand.

477
00:29:50,079 --> 00:29:53,249
We must do what's best for Sosuke.

478
00:29:54,918 --> 00:29:58,296
I want to eliminate
every possible disadvantage.

479
00:30:05,470 --> 00:30:07,138
I don't mind.

480
00:30:08,264 --> 00:30:10,892
Please take me off the case.

481
00:30:14,729 --> 00:30:16,396
<i>I'm honestly frustrated.</i>

482
00:30:16,397 --> 00:30:20,568
You were working so hard
for the client, Ms. Minamida.

483
00:30:29,619 --> 00:30:30,745
I think

484
00:30:31,496 --> 00:30:33,081
the Chairman is right.

485
00:30:34,374 --> 00:30:35,917
How so?

486
00:30:37,126 --> 00:30:41,673
When people see
you and me walking together,

487
00:30:42,715 --> 00:30:46,344
they think you're doing volunteer work
for the disabled.

488
00:30:47,428 --> 00:30:49,681
Still doing that volunteer work
for the disabled?

489
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:53,308
When Sosuke didn't pay the taxi fare,

490
00:30:53,309 --> 00:30:54,519
<i>the driver</i>

491
00:30:55,728 --> 00:30:58,982
<i>didn't think I could resolve
the situation.</i>

492
00:31:01,150 --> 00:31:05,446
I know how Sosuke and I are different

493
00:31:07,991 --> 00:31:09,951
even though we both have autism,

494
00:31:11,327 --> 00:31:13,746
but the prosecutor and the jury
won't understand.

495
00:31:15,123 --> 00:31:16,749
That's why, I...

496
00:31:20,879 --> 00:31:22,630
I can't help...

497
00:31:27,719 --> 00:31:28,761
the defendant.

498
00:31:34,267 --> 00:31:35,602
<i>In Nazi Germany,</i>

499
00:31:36,352 --> 00:31:37,979
<i>until 81 years ago,</i>

500
00:31:38,479 --> 00:31:40,355
<i>the rights of people with disabilities</i>

501
00:31:40,356 --> 00:31:43,150
<i>were stripped away through laws
and government policies,</i>

502
00:31:43,151 --> 00:31:47,155
<i>and some were killed
as lives "unworthy of life."</i>

503
00:31:48,615 --> 00:31:49,574
<i>People with</i>

504
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:53,369
<i>Autism Spectrum Disorder
were included among them.</i>

505
00:32:02,170 --> 00:32:03,129
Let's go.

506
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:11,220
<i>Sosuke and I</i>

507
00:32:11,846 --> 00:32:15,391
<i>are people whose worthiness to live
was once measured.</i>

508
00:32:16,726 --> 00:32:18,519
<i>And even now, many people</i>

509
00:32:19,312 --> 00:32:23,649
<i>press "Like" on comments
saying it is a loss to society</i>

510
00:32:23,650 --> 00:32:26,653
<i>that a bright young man died
instead of a disabled person.</i>

511
00:32:27,946 --> 00:32:32,951
<i>That's our reality
with Autism Spectrum Disorder.</i>

512
00:32:43,086 --> 00:32:44,586
Mr. Miyaji asked me

513
00:32:44,587 --> 00:32:46,672
to take over

514
00:32:46,673 --> 00:32:50,634
the Fukamachi Biotech case
from Ms. Minamida.

515
00:32:50,635 --> 00:32:52,511
Oh, really.

516
00:32:52,512 --> 00:32:54,472
Well, I'll make sure
the rest goes smoothly.

517
00:32:55,640 --> 00:32:58,768
Look forward to a treat
from the Managing Partner.

518
00:33:03,815 --> 00:33:05,024
What a jerk.

519
00:33:18,538 --> 00:33:19,622
Ms. Minamida.

520
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:22,959
I'm coming in.

521
00:33:25,586 --> 00:33:26,587
Ms. Minamida!

522
00:33:59,162 --> 00:34:02,415
Minato, your hand
is firmly grabbing my butt.

523
00:34:04,208 --> 00:34:05,168
I'm sorry.

524
00:34:10,381 --> 00:34:13,175
Minato grabbed my butt.

525
00:34:13,176 --> 00:34:16,554
Minato grabbed my butt!

526
00:34:24,979 --> 00:34:26,730
It's because of the butt-grabbing!

527
00:34:26,731 --> 00:34:27,732
Um...

528
00:34:30,735 --> 00:34:32,236
Ms. Minamida! Your shoes!

529
00:34:35,656 --> 00:34:36,615
Come in.

530
00:34:36,616 --> 00:34:37,575
Excuse me.

531
00:34:42,622 --> 00:34:43,455
What is it?

532
00:34:43,456 --> 00:34:45,082
I was hanging myself earlier...

533
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:46,833
...but Minato saved me.

534
00:34:46,834 --> 00:34:51,004
First, Minato used his left hand
to lift my butt up like this.

535
00:34:51,005 --> 00:34:53,924
Then, he tried to remove the cord
from my neck with his right hand.

536
00:34:53,925 --> 00:34:55,634
What do you think happened then?

537
00:34:55,635 --> 00:34:56,551
I have no idea.

538
00:34:56,552 --> 00:34:59,596
My body tilted back,
and I fell on my back.

539
00:34:59,597 --> 00:35:00,515
What's this about?

540
00:35:01,390 --> 00:35:04,935
The brother's cause of death
was internal bleeding from broken ribs.

541
00:35:04,936 --> 00:35:06,478
The death certificate

542
00:35:06,479 --> 00:35:09,481
stated 22 of his ribs were broken.

543
00:35:09,482 --> 00:35:13,235
Five right anterior ribs,
numbers three through seven.

544
00:35:13,236 --> 00:35:16,696
Six left anterior ribs, two through seven.

545
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:18,366
And on the back...

546
00:35:21,911 --> 00:35:24,329
um, let me borrow your ribs for a second.

547
00:35:24,330 --> 00:35:25,664
Yes, go ahead.

548
00:35:25,665 --> 00:35:26,748
11 right posterior ribs,

549
00:35:26,749 --> 00:35:29,751
numbers two through twelve.

550
00:35:29,752 --> 00:35:31,670
There were no fractures elsewhere.

551
00:35:31,671 --> 00:35:34,881
What's more, the 11 fractures
in the right posterior ribs

552
00:35:34,882 --> 00:35:36,007
form a straight line.

553
00:35:36,008 --> 00:35:37,343
Isn't that strange?

554
00:35:38,928 --> 00:35:41,471
I heard that when Sosuke
gets overstimulated,

555
00:35:41,472 --> 00:35:43,975
he keeps jumping up and down
until he calms down.

556
00:35:44,767 --> 00:35:46,393
When in a state like that,

557
00:35:46,394 --> 00:35:48,979
I think it would be
extremely difficult to punch

558
00:35:48,980 --> 00:35:51,690
his brother straight in the back
so that the ribs

559
00:35:51,691 --> 00:35:53,442
break cleanly in a straight line.

560
00:35:54,026 --> 00:35:57,654
However, it is possible
if Sosuke tried to save his older brother

561
00:35:57,655 --> 00:36:00,491
using the exact same method Minato did.

562
00:36:01,325 --> 00:36:04,870
<i>Because the defendant
firmly grabbed the victim's butt,</i>

563
00:36:04,871 --> 00:36:07,290
<i>the victim fell onto his back
on the floor.</i>

564
00:36:07,999 --> 00:36:10,167
Just like his beloved Ultraman Zero would,

565
00:36:10,168 --> 00:36:14,088
Sosuke must have been trying
to protect his brother.

566
00:36:21,053 --> 00:36:21,971
An accident?

567
00:36:22,972 --> 00:36:23,805
Yes.

568
00:36:23,806 --> 00:36:27,392
The fractures may not have been caused
by Sosuke's assault.

569
00:36:27,393 --> 00:36:29,811
And when Sosuke was straddling him,

570
00:36:29,812 --> 00:36:33,566
<i>he might have just been trying to wake up
your unconscious son.</i>

571
00:36:34,650 --> 00:36:35,693
So Sosuke...

572
00:36:37,403 --> 00:36:40,114
was trying to save his brother.

573
00:36:44,285 --> 00:36:46,494
Assault charges may
still be warranted,

574
00:36:46,495 --> 00:36:49,165
but we can clear him of suspicion
of causing death by assault.

575
00:36:53,169 --> 00:36:54,170
However...

576
00:36:54,921 --> 00:36:56,046
to do that,

577
00:36:56,047 --> 00:37:00,259
we must reveal the fact
that your eldest son attempted suicide.

578
00:37:02,345 --> 00:37:04,972
We'd like you to decide
what to do, Chairman.

579
00:37:06,390 --> 00:37:07,225
Dear...

580
00:37:10,394 --> 00:37:11,687
When you get to this age,

581
00:37:13,356 --> 00:37:16,776
your children start to feel like
a report card on your life.

582
00:37:17,944 --> 00:37:19,070
Partly because of that,

583
00:37:20,404 --> 00:37:22,323
honestly, I didn't want to admit

584
00:37:22,990 --> 00:37:25,952
that my eldest son was unhappy.

585
00:37:26,661 --> 00:37:27,578
<i>But...</i>

586
00:37:28,204 --> 00:37:30,330
I WANT TO BECOME RESPECTABLE
LIKE MY PARENTS

587
00:37:30,331 --> 00:37:33,960
I TRIED SO HARD TO GET EVEN ONE STEP
CLOSER TO THEM, SO WHY AM I LIKE THIS?

588
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:35,753
<i>He...</i>

589
00:37:36,462 --> 00:37:39,423
<i>had sensed those expectations of ours.</i>

590
00:37:43,177 --> 00:37:44,637
<i>We were the ones who pushed</i>

591
00:37:45,388 --> 00:37:47,265
<i>our son into a corner, weren't we?</i>

592
00:37:48,266 --> 00:37:50,476
If he were alive,

593
00:37:52,228 --> 00:37:53,646
I'm sure

594
00:37:55,106 --> 00:37:56,399
he would tell us this:

595
00:37:59,277 --> 00:38:00,361
"Please protect...

596
00:38:03,781 --> 00:38:04,782
my little brother."

597
00:38:05,783 --> 00:38:07,285
"Protect Sosuke."

598
00:38:11,289 --> 00:38:12,373
Please

599
00:38:14,000 --> 00:38:15,584
take care of Sosuke.

600
00:38:17,086 --> 00:38:18,170
Understood.

601
00:38:22,508 --> 00:38:23,551
Regarding that...

602
00:38:24,427 --> 00:38:25,593
Yes.

603
00:38:25,594 --> 00:38:28,138
Ms. Minamida is the one who noticed

604
00:38:28,139 --> 00:38:29,931
this was an accident.

605
00:38:29,932 --> 00:38:32,310
- As for who handles the case...
- That's...

606
00:38:37,481 --> 00:38:38,733
Ms. Minamida.

607
00:38:41,319 --> 00:38:42,486
Ms. Minamida.

608
00:38:44,030 --> 00:38:45,489
The meeting just ended.

609
00:38:46,282 --> 00:38:49,743
We're going to make
his suicide attempt public

610
00:38:49,744 --> 00:38:52,079
and argue that his death was accidental.

611
00:38:53,664 --> 00:38:55,665
I see. I'm glad.

612
00:38:55,666 --> 00:38:56,584
Yeah.

613
00:38:57,293 --> 00:39:00,087
Oh, and about who's handling the case...

614
00:39:07,345 --> 00:39:09,388
I won't be of any help,

615
00:39:10,389 --> 00:39:13,309
so please handle it, Mr. Himi.

616
00:39:14,352 --> 00:39:16,062
Ah, right.

617
00:39:17,271 --> 00:39:18,314
Leave it to me.

618
00:39:43,047 --> 00:39:44,715
Please, right this way.

619
00:39:53,391 --> 00:39:54,724
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

620
00:39:54,725 --> 00:39:56,811
AREN'T YOU COMING TO OBSERVE
THE 10 AM TRIAL?

621
00:40:03,776 --> 00:40:06,570
Minami, it's time to wake up.
I'm opening the door.

622
00:40:11,951 --> 00:40:13,243
It's already 10:00.

623
00:40:13,244 --> 00:40:14,662
I can't wash your pajamas.

624
00:40:17,498 --> 00:40:18,791
Do you have the day off?

625
00:40:20,459 --> 00:40:21,752
I'll go later.

626
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,004
It'll be noon soon.

627
00:40:34,515 --> 00:40:37,184
Now, will the defendant
please take the stand.

628
00:40:39,478 --> 00:40:41,313
Sosuke, right this way.

629
00:40:41,897 --> 00:40:42,731
Yes.

630
00:40:44,442 --> 00:40:45,317
Sosuke!

631
00:40:47,153 --> 00:40:48,112
Right this way.

632
00:40:48,612 --> 00:40:49,447
Yes.

633
00:40:55,327 --> 00:40:58,122
Next is the defendant's questioning,

634
00:40:58,622 --> 00:41:02,918
but please allow me to ask him
some questions first.

635
00:41:03,711 --> 00:41:04,795
Defendant.

636
00:41:06,464 --> 00:41:08,299
Sosuke Fukamachi.

637
00:41:09,592 --> 00:41:10,593
Yes.

638
00:41:11,093 --> 00:41:13,679
You heard the defense attorney's
statement, right?

639
00:41:14,430 --> 00:41:17,725
Did you, the defendant,
lower your brother to the floor?

640
00:41:20,311 --> 00:41:21,395
Yes.

641
00:41:23,147 --> 00:41:26,192
Did you try to save your brother?

642
00:41:28,777 --> 00:41:29,611
Yes!

643
00:41:29,612 --> 00:41:33,114
The electrical cord
didn't just come off on its own.

644
00:41:33,115 --> 00:41:34,033
Yes...

645
00:41:35,284 --> 00:41:37,076
Please answer clearly.

646
00:41:37,077 --> 00:41:41,123
Was it you who lowered your brother?
Or was it not?

647
00:41:48,923 --> 00:41:49,840
<i>Yes!</i>

648
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:01,893
<i>Sosuke Fukamachi.</i>

649
00:42:01,894 --> 00:42:05,188
You tried to save your brother.
Is that right?

650
00:42:05,189 --> 00:42:06,482
Or is it not?

651
00:42:26,794 --> 00:42:28,045
Yes!

652
00:42:38,639 --> 00:42:39,723
You did great.

653
00:42:40,724 --> 00:42:42,600
Well, we presented our argument,

654
00:42:42,601 --> 00:42:44,978
and the jury's reaction was good.

655
00:42:44,979 --> 00:42:48,565
I doubt he'll be convicted
of causing death by assault.

656
00:42:48,566 --> 00:42:51,442
Even if he gets convicted of assault
over the facial injuries,

657
00:42:51,443 --> 00:42:53,362
he'll probably get a suspended sentence.

658
00:42:53,862 --> 00:42:54,863
I'm so glad.

659
00:42:57,992 --> 00:42:59,451
Thank you very much.

660
00:43:00,077 --> 00:43:01,035
It's all thanks to you.

661
00:43:01,036 --> 00:43:01,996
Not at all.

662
00:43:03,289 --> 00:43:04,289
Things ended

663
00:43:04,290 --> 00:43:06,709
in an impolite manner this time,

664
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:10,295
but I hope you'll pass on
our thanks to Ms. Minamida as well.

665
00:43:10,296 --> 00:43:11,462
Understood.

666
00:43:11,463 --> 00:43:14,757
I imagine she's also wondering
how the trial turned out.

667
00:43:14,758 --> 00:43:17,594
I'll contact Ms. Minamida myself.

668
00:43:17,595 --> 00:43:19,680
Please do.

669
00:43:20,889 --> 00:43:21,849
Let's go.

670
00:43:33,861 --> 00:43:34,945
You got me!

671
00:43:35,571 --> 00:43:36,405
You did it!

672
00:43:44,538 --> 00:43:45,831
- Then let's go.
- Okay.

673
00:43:49,209 --> 00:43:51,545
ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

674
00:44:45,683 --> 00:44:47,059
Ms. Minamida...

675
00:44:50,729 --> 00:44:55,734
Subtitle translation by:
Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

676
00:44:56,443 --> 00:44:57,777
<i>You should stay a lawyer.</i>

677
00:44:57,778 --> 00:45:00,988
I think Ririi would be happy
if you defended her.

678
00:45:00,989 --> 00:45:02,782
<i>Can't we support her somehow?</i>

679
00:45:02,783 --> 00:45:03,699
Unfortunately.

680
00:45:03,700 --> 00:45:05,576
<i>I can't help Ririi.</i>

681
00:45:05,577 --> 00:45:07,745
<i>Going to court
is an overreaction, isn't it?</i>

682
00:45:07,746 --> 00:45:10,665
Because you've always swept things
under the rug, it's come to this!

683
00:45:10,666 --> 00:45:13,961
I believe you're a fine lawyer,
Ms. Minamida.

684
00:45:15,003 --> 00:45:16,671
I want to help you, Ririi.

685
00:45:16,672 --> 00:45:17,756
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
